  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed dormer and skylight, by reason of poor design and cumulative excessive development at roof level, would result in a development that is awkward, incongruous, visually cluttered and conflicts with the architectural industrial heritage of the building. There is not clear and convincing justification for this harm, nor public benefits to outweigh it contrary to the requirements of the National Planning Policy Framework. The development would therefore be harmful to the character and appearance of the host building and would harm the character and appearance of the Harrow on the Hill Conservation Area and the setting of the grade II listed buildings of the Old Pye House and Mission Hall, contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2021),  Policies D3(D(1) and D(11)) and HC1 of The London Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1 (B) of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policies DM1 and DM7 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010) and the Harrow on the Hill Conservation Area Appraisal and Management Strategy (2008)."
  ],
